---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Editorial Policy"
	description="How Aderonke Wellness chooses topics, sources claims, and keeps content current."
>
	<article class="aw-container aw-section">
		<h1>Editorial Policy</h1>
		<div class="aw-article-body">
			<h2>Who writes and reviews this content</h2>
			<p>Every article on this site is written or medically reviewed by Aderonke Agboji, RN, PhD Candidate in Health Sciences (Dementia Studies). See the <a href="/about/">About</a> page for her full background.</p>

			<h2>How topics are chosen</h2>
			<p>Topics come from real questions raised by caregivers, long-term care residents, and families: through conversations in care settings, reader emails, and common search questions people bring to this site. We prioritize topics where clear, accurate information is hardest to find.</p>

			<h2>How claims are sourced</h2>
			<p>Clinical or research claims are linked to their original source wherever possible: peer-reviewed journals, the National Institute on Aging, the Alzheimer’s Association, or other recognized health authorities. We avoid restating secondhand claims we can’t trace to a primary source.</p>

			<h2>When content is updated</h2>
			<p>Articles are reviewed periodically and updated when guidance changes or new research is published. Every article shows a "last updated" date so you know how current it is.</p>

			<h2>What this site is not</h2>
			<p>This site provides general educational information. It is not a substitute for individualized medical, psychological, or legal advice, and reading it does not create a clinical relationship with Aderonke Agboji or this site. See our <a href="/disclaimer/">Disclaimer</a> for more detail.</p>

			<h2>Corrections</h2>
			<p>If you spot something inaccurate or out of date, please <a href="/contact/">contact us</a>. We take corrections seriously and will review and update the article promptly.</p>
		</div>
	</article>
</BaseLayout>
